ans by about six points. That lean collides with a national environment that has favored Democrats, leaving the race close. Most professional ratings call it Lean Republican, two call it a Tossup, and prediction markets give Honeycutt roughly a 60 percent chance.\n\nPolling is sparse and sponsor-conflicted: Democratic-aligned surveys in October put Lacore up two to three points, while a Republican-aligned poll had Honeycutt up six. Lacore has raised far more money but has little cash left, and outside groups have spent somewhat more on Honeycutt's behalf. The net expectation is a narrow Republican edge, well within the range where turnout and the final week of advertising could decide it.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2812, "margin": -3.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2869, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3426, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2761, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3368, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2774, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2992, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2787, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3431, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3379, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2427, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2624, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2319, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2563, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2582, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2076, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.283, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.313, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.3